<title>ITALY: Italian Btps end sharply lower, dollar weighs.</title>
<headline>Italian Btps end sharply lower, dollar weighs.</headline>
<text>
<p>1555 GMT - Italy's debt market ended sharply lower on the effects of a strong dollar and profit-taking, the second consecutive session which saw Btp futures slide more than other European bond markets.</p>
<p>* Bonds:Feb07 -57bps at 101.98, yield 6.56, Bund spread 93</p>
<p>* Futures:SepLIF -78bps at 135.51. Sup 135.33, res 135.60</p>
<p>* Lira:firm vs mark at 970.95/1.25</p>
</text>
